  "description": "Text rules shared by both apps. Spec: docs/protocol.md, \"Text messages\": the sender's size threshold, line ends, and the sensitive flag. Strings use \\u escapes for every non-ASCII character.",
  "specVersion": 1,
  "senderThresholdBytes": 131072,
  "howToRead": "lineEndings[]: toWire(clipboardText) must equal wire (every CRLF becomes LF in one left-to-right pass; a lone CR stays), windowsClipboard is what a Windows receiver writes for that wire text (every LF not preceded by a CR becomes CRLF), and wireSha256Hex is the SHA-256 of the UTF-8 bytes of the wire form: the loop guard hashes that, never the clipboard form. A case without clipboardText only checks the receiver direction. senderSize[]: decideSend(kind, sensitive, wireBytes) must equal expected. kind text is an explicit send, clipboard the automatic one. expected: text (a text message), file (a .txt file transfer), clipboard (a clipboard message), too_large (an automatic clipboard that is not sent: status too_large) or not_sent (a sensitive text over the threshold). wireBytes is the UTF-8 size after the line-end conversion; a case with synthesize builds the text as fill repeated fillCount times (+ suffix), and rawBytes is its size before the conversion. sensitiveSender[]: what a sender does, by category, with a fake clipboard that offers the listed formats (a string is a format that is present, an object a value format with its DWORD): expect.send is text, clipboard or none, and expect.sensitive the flag on the text. receiver[]: what a receiver does with a text frame, by category, with a fake clipboard, notifier and history.",
